## STRATEGIC IMPLICATIONS

### Naive Strategy (Ignoring Treasury)
- Hold cash idle
- Pay 0.1% daily penalty
- Miss treasury yields
- **Result**: -10% to -20% from idle cash drag

### Sophisticated Strategy (Active Treasury)
- Forecast cash needs
- Ladder T-bills for liabilities
- Use overnight repo for flexibility
- Time asset sales for liquidity
- **Result**: +3-4% from treasury yields

**Differentiation**: 15-25% score difference based on treasury management alone!

### Comparison to Year 2

**Year 2** (Tax Efficiency):
- High gross returns (53%) could absorb tax burden
- Tax efficiency was important but not critical

**Year 3** (Treasury Management):
- Lower gross returns (9-13%) make every basis point count
- Treasury returns (2.5-4%) can add 2-4% to portfolio
- Idle cash penalties (36.5% annualized) are catastrophic
- Liquidity management is CRITICAL

### Portfolio Coordination

**Year 1-2 mechanics remain relevant**:
- Asset sales → generate cash (player-controlled)
- Tax payments → cash outflows (player-controlled timing)
- Valuations → affect liquidity needs
- Transaction costs → impact cash planning

**New layer**:
- Treasury instruments → deploy excess cash
- Cash flows → automatic inflows/outflows
- Liquidity planning → forecast and manage
- Zero-cash mandate → no idle cash allowed

